              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to announce, then the German for to make public."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: das Gerücht",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "das Gerücht — \"the rumour\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Im Dorf gab es ein Gerücht über den neuen Nachbarn. In the village there was a rumour about the new neighbour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Gerüchte."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Gerücht is usually traced to Middle Low German gerüchte \"outcry, talk\", built on the root of rufen \"to call\", from Proto-Germanic hrōpaną (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
