          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "behaupten — \"to claim, to assert\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Er behauptete, dass er nichts gesehen hatte. He claimed that he had seen nothing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often with dass and the verb at the end. Reflexive, sich behaupten means to hold one's own."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "behaupten is usually traced to Middle High German behoubeten \"to hold one's ground\", built on Haupt \"head\", a cousin of English head (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
